332
00:30:19,160 --> 00:30:23,520
The discovery of an ancient text can be a historian's dream.

333
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:28,880
In the case of the Archimedes polymcest,

334
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:32,760
historians also discovered an iron gall ink treasure

335
00:30:32,761 --> 00:30:35,920
hidden under layers of less significant information.

336
00:30:35,921 --> 00:30:44,140
a polymcest is basically a book whose text has been erased and overwritten

337
00:30:44,141 --> 00:30:50,800
sort of an early recycling program necessary because parchment wasn't cheap

338
00:30:50,801 --> 00:30:59,020
first the original book was taken apart an acidic solution like lemon juice or

339
00:30:59,021 --> 00:31:05,080
milk was applied to dissolve some of the ink remaining ink residue was scraped off

340
00:31:05,081 --> 00:31:06,540
with a knife or stone.

341
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:09,840
Then the pages were rotated 90 degrees,

342
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,140
written over with a new text,

343
00:31:13,060 --> 00:31:13,760
and rebound.

344
00:31:15,660 --> 00:31:20,540
The Archimedes' Palimpsest contains seven theorems of Archimedes.

345
00:31:20,820 --> 00:31:23,000
The most important one is called the method.

346
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:27,960
The method doesn't survive in any other copy of Archimedes' works,

347
00:31:27,961 --> 00:31:32,080
and so that's why this palimpsest is so important.

348
00:31:32,081 --> 00:31:39,800
Hidden beneath this text is a copy of Archimedes' 3rd century B.C. theorems,

349
00:31:40,980 --> 00:31:44,540
written in Greek by a Byzantine scribe around A.D. 950.

350
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:50,160
Monks palimpsested it into a prayer book in the 13th century.

351
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:55,080
And to add insult to injury...

352
00:31:55,081 --> 00:32:01,080
In the 20th century, at least four of the pages were overpainted with forged paintings

353
00:32:01,081 --> 00:32:04,120
paintings to make them look as though they'd been

354
00:32:04,121 --> 00:32:08,260
painted in medieval times. This was apparently an attempt

355
00:32:08,261 --> 00:32:12,800
to increase the value of the book because art was considered to be more valuable

356
00:32:12,801 --> 00:32:15,360
than manuscripts.

357
00:32:15,361 --> 00:32:18,400
The Palimpsest's owner, an anonymous collector,

358
00:32:18,401 --> 00:32:22,080
entrusted it to the Stanford Synchrotron Radiation Lab

359
00:32:22,081 --> 00:32:26,580
and the Walters Art Museum for imaging and conservation.

360
00:32:26,581 --> 00:32:35,720
At the center of the project was the iron gall ink used to record Archimedes work and

361
00:32:35,721 --> 00:32:41,640
the vast network of imaging technology used to make it reappear.

362
00:32:41,641 --> 00:32:46,760
My usual research is on spinach and the whole experiment started with the question, what

363
00:32:46,761 --> 00:32:52,140
is spinach in common with the Archimedes hypothesis?

364
00:32:52,141 --> 00:32:57,580
determined that the x-ray technique used to study trace metals in spinach could be used to image

365
00:32:57,581 --> 00:33:02,042
hidden or faint iron gall ink in the polymcest.

366
00:33:02,043 --> 00:33:06,220
When you excite any element with x-rays, the

367
00:33:06,221 --> 00:33:12,260
element will send out a fluorescence glow, and we are recording that glow with our detectors.

368
00:33:12,261 --> 00:33:18,320
We can tune our detector so that we only see one particular element, because each element in the

369
00:33:18,321 --> 00:33:24,400
periodic table, let's say iron or manganese or chlorine or calcium, they all send out

370
00:33:24,401 --> 00:33:28,380
this glow at a different color and our detector can pick up that color.

371
00:33:28,381 --> 00:33:33,600
And so rather than seeing everything which is on the book, we only see the iron and we

372
00:33:33,601 --> 00:33:39,080
know that the iron is mostly only in the ink, so we can create an X-ray image just of the

373
00:33:39,081 --> 00:33:43,000
ink in this book.

374
00:33:43,001 --> 00:33:49,400
The hair-thin x-ray beam scans the page, and the historic writings held therein appear on the screen.

375
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:57,560
Once the two sets of writing are digitally processed, Archimedes' work is translated and deciphered.

376
00:33:58,320 --> 00:34:04,140
We now believe that Archimedes understood the basic principles of mathematical calculus

377
00:34:04,141 --> 00:34:10,120
1,800 years before Newton and Leibniz came up with their demonstrations in the 1600s.

378
00:34:10,121 --> 00:34:15,940
And that is completely revolutionizing the place of Archimedes in the history of mathematics.

379
00:34:17,740 --> 00:34:24,000
Examining groundbreaking 1,000-year-old historical documents is one reason for forensic technology.

380
00:34:25,700 --> 00:34:30,960
But in the modern world, there are other reasons to scrutinize and analyze writing samples.

381
00:34:34,620 --> 00:34:38,486
State and local law enforcement officials often collaborate with the U.S.

382
00:34:38,487 --> 00:34:39,280
Secret Service.

383
00:34:40,120 --> 00:34:42,360
and their Forensic Services Inc.

384
00:34:42,361 --> 00:34:46,280
Library to help solve crimes involving suspect writings.

385
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:54,440
Any crime that involves ink or paper where the ink is on the paper, whether it be a question

386
00:34:54,441 --> 00:35:01,320
document, a ransom note for example, some sort of a message that might lead us to the perpetrator

387
00:35:01,321 --> 00:35:08,840
or lead us to the victim, such as homicide, such as extortion, such as kidnapping, sometimes rape,

388
00:35:08,841 --> 00:35:12,620
robbery, obviously question documents, fraud, identity theft.

389
00:35:13,740 --> 00:35:17,240
The library contains nearly 10,000 ink samples,

390
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:19,780
some in bottles, some in pens,

391
00:35:20,100 --> 00:35:22,480
dating back to the 1920s.

392
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:27,640
Investigators use a series of tests

393
00:35:27,641 --> 00:35:30,380
to determine the writing instrument and ink used,

394
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:35,200
as well as a time frame during which a question document could have been produced.

395
00:35:35,201 --> 00:35:39,640
The first thing we do is magnification.

396
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:50,300
We use a microscopic exam where we try to determine whether it be a ballpoint writing instrument or a non-ballpoint writing instrument.

397
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:55,960
At that point, we move to the next test, which involves optical exams.

398
00:35:56,180 --> 00:36:01,980
We actually put the ink under different lighting conditions because ink reflect light differently.

399
00:36:01,981 --> 00:36:05,860
The third test is the thin layer chromatography.

400
00:36:06,620 --> 00:36:11,040
This actually gives us the chemical formulation of the ink in question.

401
00:36:12,620 --> 00:36:15,120
This looks like a normal everyday check.

402
00:36:16,820 --> 00:36:19,820
But investigators can easily spot a counterfeit check

403
00:36:19,821 --> 00:36:24,420
by using optical equipment to filter out different portions of the light spectrum

404
00:36:24,421 --> 00:36:28,260
and watching for ink reflection inconsistencies.

405
00:36:28,261 --> 00:36:32,100
Gotcha.

406
00:36:34,740 --> 00:36:40,320
In thin layer chromatography, investigators remove ink samples from the forged check

407
00:36:40,321 --> 00:36:43,440
and introduce the ink into a solvent.

408
00:36:47,140 --> 00:36:51,660
The ink becomes liquid, which allows them to chemically analyze and match the sample

409
00:36:51,661 --> 00:36:54,440
to one of the thousands of ink formulas in the library.

410
00:36:54,441 --> 00:37:02,220
With this information, now it gives our case investigators a significant amount of leads.

411
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:06,080
It can tell us not only when the ink was manufactured,

412
00:37:06,420 --> 00:37:10,540
but it can give us an approximation as to when the crime actually was committed.

413
00:37:10,860 --> 00:37:15,120
If we happen to have suspects, for example, and we do a search warrant,

414
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:20,760
we can actually obtain writing inks that that suspect might be in possession of

415
00:37:20,761 --> 00:37:27,440
or might have had access to, either in his residence, in his place of business, or in some other environment.

416
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:33,260
Ink can take on many jobs, including historian and crime fighter.

417
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:39,060
But when worn on the skin, it's an artist, biographer, even lifesaver.

